**RULES SECTION OF THE PROGRAM IF NEEDED > README (optional)**

A rules file tells hashcat how to mutate each word in your wordlist before trying it. 
So instead of just trying password, hashcat will also try Password, p@ssword, password1, PASSWORD, etc., all derived from the same base word automatically.

*Why it matters for CTFs*
Wordlists alone (even rockyou) miss a lot. Most real passwords aren't dictionary words exactly. People like to capitalize, add numbers, swap letters for symbols. Rules bridge that gap without needing a bigger wordlist.
